# TG BRCA RNA-seq pipeline (downregulation, six designs)

## Data
- Dir: `E:/R/TG_BRCA/TG` (fallback: script/repo dir)
- Input: Cuffdiff `genes.read_group_tracking`, then `genes.count_tracking` / `genes.fpkm_tracking`
- Samples: `NTC_rep0`, `NTC_rep1`, `TG_sh1`, `TG_sh5`
- Human `org.Hs.eg.db`
- Cufflinks `gene_short_name` may be fused (`SAA2,SAA2-SAA4,SAA4`) or locus IDs (`XLOC_######`). Clean to one official symbol; keep remaining XLOC rows for DE but they will not map in GO/KEGG.

## Preprocess (once, all samples together)
Filter low expression, then normalize (DESeq2 size factors if counts; quantile log2 if FPKM).

## Six designs (each gets its own plots; never merge NTC_rep0 with NTC_rep1 except design 2)
1. Pairwise 1-vs-1, separately: `TG_sh1 vs NTC_rep0`, `TG_sh5 vs NTC_rep0`, `TG_sh1 vs NTC_rep1`, `TG_sh5 vs NTC_rep1`. log2FC from normalized values; no p-value (1 vs 1).
2. Combined: mean(TG_sh1, TG_sh5) vs NTC group mean(NTC_rep0, NTC_rep1). Equal weight to the two knockdowns.
3. Common down vs NTC_rep0: intersection of downregulated genes from `TG_sh1 vs NTC_rep0` and `TG_sh5 vs NTC_rep0`.
4. Common down vs NTC_rep1: intersection of downregulated genes from `TG_sh1 vs NTC_rep1` and `TG_sh5 vs NTC_rep1`.
5. mean(TG_sh1, TG_sh5) vs NTC_rep0 (FC only).
6. mean(TG_sh1, TG_sh5) vs NTC_rep1 (FC only).

## Subset grid (every design, do not skip a cutoff)
- FC down: treat/control ≤ 1, 0.8, 0.6, 0.5 (folders `FC_1` / `FC_0.8` / `FC_0.6` / `FC_0.5`)
- Top down: 50, 75, 100, 150, 200, 250, 300 (most negative log2FC)
- Pairwise / common / designs 5–6: FC/rank only. Design 2: `padj < 0.05` if estimable, else FC/rank only.

## Plots in every non-empty subset
- DE table, volcano, heatmap
- ORA (单独的 GO / 通路 / KEGG，不是 GSEA): `GO/`, `Pathway/`, `KEGG/`, filenames start with `ORA_`
- GSEA: `GSEA/` and `00_GSEA_all_genes_NOT_FC_or_topN`, filenames start with `GSEA_`
- Do not inflate genome-wide GO/KEGG p-values. Cytoskeleton-motility and mitochondria hypotheses go in `Focused_cytoskeleton_mito/` (custom gene-set GSEA/ORA).
